IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`
IMPORT `lhl-rules`
IMPORT `lhl-seat-worker`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- worked cases for the worker's questions (lhl-seat-worker.l4). Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `worker cases`

`contractor management` MEANS `a business of providing contractor management services`
`other business` MEANS `another business`
`supply` MEANS `wholly or principally the supply of labour`
`placing` MEANS `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person`
`9(1)` MEANS `a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it`
`9(2)(a)` MEANS `a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them for the work`
`9(2)(b)` MEANS `a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance`

§§ `ss 9, 11 -- am I a worker`

#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `9(1)` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `9(2)(a)` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `9(2)(b)` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `none of these` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a labour hire worker` `9(1)` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 7 to 10, 13 -- is the business unlicensed`

-- Arguments: business, character, engagement, accommodation, s 10 exclusion, s 11 exclusion, licence in force.
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `contractor management` `placing` `9(2)(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` `other business` `placing` `9(2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 46 -- seeing the licence`

#ASSERT `Must my provider show me its licence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my provider show me its licence` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 86 -- threats and detriment`

#ASSERT `Is what was done to me forbidden` `I was dismissed, or my employment, hiring or engagement was terminated` `because of information under the Act that I gave or intended to give, or to stop me giving it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me forbidden` `I was refused employment, hire or engagement` `because of a requirement under the Act I complied with or intended to comply with, or to stop me complying` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me forbidden` `I was threatened or intimidated` `because of a process under the Act I took part in or intended to take part in, or to stop me continuing it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me forbidden` `I was subjected to another detriment` `for another reason` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me forbidden` `nothing of that kind` `because of information under the Act that I gave or intended to give, or to stop me giving it` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be ordered to pay` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be ordered to pay` TRUE TRUE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be ordered to pay` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be ordered to pay` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 200
